    WI-104: pin the meta dev toolchain (requirements-dev.txt + CI/dev-setup consume + canary)
    
    M6 from the 2026-07-12b review: the kit runtime is dependency-free, but the
    meta-repo's own verification chain floated on unpinned dev tools, so the same
    declared command ran different machinery per machine (the concrete cost being
    M9's flaky coverage race on this box's old pytest-cov 4.1.0 vs CI's 7.x).
    
    - New root requirements-dev.txt: compatible-release (~=) pins for ruff, pytest,
      pytest-xdist, and a Python-gated pytest-cov split (~=7.0 on 3.9+, ~=5.0 on the
      3.8 floor, since pytest-cov 6.0 dropped 3.8 - the one irreducible per-Python
      difference WI-105 must harden across).
    - Consumers rewired to `pip install -r requirements-dev.txt`: both test.yml jobs
      (test + gate) and both meta dev-setup twins (dev-setup.sh/.ps1); the .command
      wrapper delegates unchanged.
    - New canary.yml: non-gating weekly (+ workflow_dispatch) job installs UNPINNED
      latest and runs ruff format/lint + the suite, preserving the early-warning the
      unpinned CI gave for free so a pin bump is a heads-up, not a surprise red.
    
    Scope held: kit scripts stay stdlib-only, nothing ships downstream
    (project-trajectory/scripts/setup.* + ci/check.yml are the adopter's own
    templates, untouched). No spine change; no byte-budgeted file touched.
    
    Verified on the pinned 3.8 resolution in a throwaway venv (pytest 8.3.5,
    pytest-cov 5.0.0, ruff 0.15.21, xdist 3.6.1, coverage 7.6.1): full suite 695
    passed / 3 skipped, ruff format+lint clean, smoke 543 passed, check_docs --stale
    + check_trajectory --strict clean, gen_trajectory --check up to date.
    
    docs/next-wi -> WI-105 (coverage-plumbing fix, now verifiable on the pinned
    toolchain). Not pushed (push-policy: human).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

